    <!-- The disclosure before the first online lookup. -->
    <string name="identification_disclosure_title">Online identification</string>
    <string name="identification_disclosure_intro">To identify your tracks, PiPlayer can look them up in online music databases. Nothing is sent until you choose Enable. This is what each service gets:</string>
    <string name="identification_sends_acoustid">AcoustID gets audio fingerprints and track lengths. The audio itself never leaves your device.</string>
    <string name="identification_sends_musicbrainz">MusicBrainz gets the tags already in your files, words from their file names, track lengths and MusicBrainz IDs.</string>
    <string name="identification_sends_caa">Cover Art Archive gets release and release group IDs, and so does archive.org, where it keeps the images. This also happens in the background: while albums without a cover of their own are shown in lists, PiPlayer asks for their covers.</string>
    <string name="identification_sends_all">Every service sees your IP address and PiPlayer\'s user agent: the app\'s name, its version and the project\'s address.</string>
    <string name="identification_disclosure_local">With Not now, identification stays on this device and uses only what your files already hold. You can change this at any time in Settings, Identification and privacy.</string>
